      "description": "Watch Lyon vs Fenerbahce highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 26, 2026. The Groupama Stadium played host to a high-stakes encounter as Olympique Lyonnais and Fenerbahce faced off in the UEFA Champions League . Both sides entered the pitch with everything to play for in what promised to be a defining night of European football. Clinical First Half from the Visitors On 2026-08-26 , the match began with immediate intensity as the visitors sought to dominate early. Fenerbahce broke the deadlock in the 24th minute when Vedat Muriqi found the back of the net with a clinical finish. The momentum stayed firmly with the Turkish side, and just four minutes later, Archie Brown doubled the lead after a precise assist from Mason Greenwood . Lyon struggled to regain their composure, and the physical nature of the contest became evident when Milan Skriniar received a yellow card in the 32nd minute. Lyon Fight Back Amid Late Drama The second half saw Lyon emerge with renewed energy, despite an early booking for Ikoma Lois Openda . Their efforts were rewarded in the 61st minute when Malick Fofana clinicaly finished a chance created by Ainsley Maitland-Niles , pulling the score back to 1-2. A flurry of substitutions followed, with the likes of Nicolas Tagliafico and Romelu Lukaku entering the fray to influence the closing stages. The match ended in a heated fashion, with Matteo Guendouzi and Dorgeles Nene both receiving yellow cards deep in stoppage time, but Fenerbahce successfully defended their lead until the final whistle."
